    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0811" n="781" xml:id="pg781"/>

                <head>335. Memorandum From Secretary of State Rusk to President Johnson<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d335-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1968-11-07">November 7, 1968</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>The Forthcoming NATO Ministerial
                        Meeting</item>
                </list>
                <p>Secretary Fowler, Secretary Clifford, General Wheeler and I will be
                    attending the NATO Ministerial sessions in
                    Brussels, November 12 through 14. As you know, the main focus of the meeting
                    will be on what our Allies and we should do to strengthen NATO in the light of the Warsaw Pact invasion of
                    Czechoslovakia.</p>
                <p>We anticipate that the meeting will reflect the groundwork laid since our
                    September 4 discussion in the National Security Council.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d335-f2"/> Our ambassadors have made vigorous demarches regarding
                    improved allied defense contributions. Ambassador Cleveland has been involved in continuous negotiations with his
                    colleagues in NATO and I had discussions with
                    most NATO foreign ministers in New York.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d335-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>I enclose a listing of the main issues that may arise at the meeting. You may
                    wish to discuss these with us prior to our departure.</p>
                <p>I also enclose (1) a paper outlining the background and scope of the Ministerial
                    Meeting; and (2) a paper summarizing what we are doing with each NATO country to encourage improved defense
                        efforts.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d335-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Dean Rusk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d335-a1.xml" xpointer="d335-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
